{
 "schema": 1,
 "note": "Binds a documented integer to the code that emits it -- a schema or API version, or a published bound such as the grid ceiling. A document states the integer with a <!-- conformance:version id=N --> marker and never in prose, because several historical sentences in the canonical documents cite old versions correctly and a prose scrape cannot tell the difference. Resolver kinds: constant, cxx-constexpr, emitted-key, returned-key, tuple-bound (an entry of a bounds table, bounds={'size':(3,1025)}) and call-arg (an integer argument of a named call, selected by another constant argument -- the guard half of a published bound). Any binding may carry a `mirror` naming a second statement of the same fact; the two are resolved independently and reported when they disagree. No binding uses cxx-constexpr any more: the three planner VERSION-MIRROR clauses tying Python to Core/*.hpp planner_version were removed on 2026-09-21 as follow-through on decision 027, which rules that native divergence is not a defect, is not tracked, and is not a hold on anything. The resolver still supports the kind; nothing should use it before the port is scoped again. An emitted-key binding is additionally scanned for across every module under Sim/, so a second site writing the same block with a different integer is reported rather than guessed at.",
