   "mirror_note": "Not a schema version: a published bound, bound here for the same reason. The registry advertises the grid range in its `bounds` table and a separate statement of the same integer four hundred lines below rejects a world outside it. They agreed because somebody checked, which is the footing the Python and native grid ceilings were on before they drifted from 257 to 1025 with nothing published saying so. The `code` side reads the advertised bound out of the table and the `mirror` side reads the guard's own argument, so the two cannot move apart without a VERSION-MIRROR finding naming both. Deriving the guard from the table in terrain_world.py would be better still and is one line; it was not done here because that file is provenance-pinned and the edit needs a manifest revision row this lane does not own. See board/done/PRODUCT-PARAMETER-PROVENANCE.md.",
